; gen2_tag.loom
; An EPC Gen2 UHF RFID tag (ISO/IEC 18000-63) at baseband: it decodes the
; reader's PIE commands from the demodulated envelope, calibrates its own
; decoder and its own backscatter clock from the command's preamble, and
; answers Query with an RN16 and ACK with PC + EPC + PacketCRC, in FM0 or in
; Miller-M (M = 2, 4, 8), with the preamble and pilot tone the Query asks for.
;
; Written on 2026-11-25, after the hardware was complete (D-032), as a
; protocol Loom was not designed for (D-035). Nothing in Loom was built for
; RFID. The program times the reader's symbols with the level waits
; (`WAITP`, built for I2C and SPI, with the deadline timeout `T` as the end
; of a frame) and reads of the `NOW` tick counter (the deadline timebase,
; SEMANTICS 4); it checks the Query's CRC-5 and computes the PacketCRC with
; the bit engine's CRC (6.9, built for USB and CAN; `SHO` on pin index 15,
; which drives no pin); it puts its backscatter edges on the tick with the
; deadline-latched pin write (`SETP ... D`, 6.10, built for exact edges) and
; turns the tick itself into its link clock: TICK_INT/TICK_FRAC (built for
; UART baud rates) are written at run time with half a backscatter cycle,
; computed from the TRcal it measured. Parameters and the reply words live in
; the data memory (`LD`/`ST`, 6.11, built for device emulation).
; What the firmware does that no hardware does: the PIE decoder and its
; self-calibration (pivot = RTcal / 2, 6.3.1.2.8), the BLF arithmetic
; (BLF = DR / TRcal, eq. 1), the FM0 and Miller coders (one toggle rule for
; both, below), the preambles, the T1 timing, the RN16 and the tag's states.
;
; Baseband only. ENV = IN0 is the reader's demodulated RF envelope as a
; logic level: high = CW, low = the reader's modulated pulse (PW, the
; delimiter). BS = OUT0 is the backscatter modulator: 1 = the reflecting
; state of the first high of a preamble, 0 = the state during CW before a
; reply (6.3.1.3). There is no RF here: a front end demodulates and switches.
;
; Sources (tools/protomodels/gen2.py cites them item by item): GS1 EPC Gen2
; UHF RFID Standard, Release 3.0.1, Feb 2026: 6.3.1.2.3 (PIE), 6.3.1.2.4
; (Tari), Table 6-5 (PW), 6.3.1.2.8 and Figure 6-4 (preamble, frame-sync,
; RTcal, pivot, TRcal, eq. 1 and 2), 6.3.1.3.2.1-4 and Figures 6-8 to 6-15
; (FM0, Miller, dummy bit, preambles), Table 6-9 (BLF tolerances), Table 6-10
; (M), 6.3.1.5 and Tables 6-11, 6-12, Annex F.1 (CRC-16, CRC-5), 6.3.1.6
; Table 6-16 (T1), 6.3.2.12.2.1 Table 6-33/6-34 (Query, RN16), 6.3.2.12.2.6
; Table 6-46 (ACK), Table 6-18 and 6.3.2.1.2.1 (PC, EPC, PacketCRC).
;
; Reception (tick 1 clock). A frame is timed rising edge to rising edge (the
; end of each PW): the delimiter's rise, then data-0 (Tari), then RTcal,
; then either TRcal (longer than RTcal: a preamble) or the first data bit (a
; frame-sync). An interval i is a data-1 when 2i >= RTcal (pivot = RTcal/2).
; No falling edge within 1.5 RTcal of the last rise ends the frame (a data
; symbol is shorter than RTcal, T4 between commands is 2 RTcal); while TRcal
; may still come the wait is 3 RTcal (eq. 2). A bad CRC-5 Query, an ACK
; with the wrong RN16 and an ACK with no RN16 out all leave the tag silent
; in arbitrate (6.3.2.12.2.1, 6.3.2.12.2.6; for the bad Query, Table C-34
; was not read: arbitrate is this program's reading). Commands
; are told by their first bits: 01 = ACK (18 bits), 1000 = Query (22 bits);
; any other frame is skipped to its end. The delimiter's length is not
; checked (it overlaps PW at Tari 25 us); RTcal is not checked against Tari.
;
; Reply (tick = half a backscatter cycle). DR = 8: TRcal / 16 clocks; DR =
; 64/3: 3 TRcal / 128 clocks, in 1/256 clocks (stamp error +-8 clocks, 0.3 %
; at TRcal 50 us, against +-7 % or more in Table 6-9). Half periods shorter
; than HMIN clocks (BLF above about 225 kHz at 45 MHz) are refused: the tag
; stays silent. The first rising edge comes T1 = MAX(RTcal, 10 Tpri) after
; the last rising edge of the command (Table 6-16), within a slot. Each half
; cycle the line either toggles or holds. FM0: toggle at every symbol
; boundary and in the middle of a data-0. Miller-M (2M halves a bit): toggle
; at every half, except at the middle of a data-1 and at the boundary between
; two data-0s (the baseband inversion cancels the subcarrier's). Preambles:
; FM0 the 12-half toggle pattern of "1 0 1 0 v 1" (Figure 6-11), after 12
; zeros if TRext; Miller 4 M (16 M if TRext) halves of pilot then 010111
; (Figure 6-15). Every reply ends with the dummy 1, then BS returns to 0.
;
; Host words (INQ thread 0), after RUN: 1. the RN16 seed; 2. N, EPC words
; (1..8); 3. the N EPC words. PC = N << 11 (UMI, XI, T, AFI 0); PacketCRC =
; ~CRC-16 over PC and EPC, computed once. Nothing is reported on OUTQ.
;
; Limits, honestly: only Query and ACK. Sel, Session and Target are not
; evaluated (the tag answers every Query); the slot counter is drawn from Q,
; and a tag whose slot is not 0 stays silent for the round (no QueryRep or
; QueryAdjust, no inventoried flags). An ACK with the wrong RN16 sends it
; back to arbitrate; an ACK with no Query before it is ignored. No QueryX,
; no extended preamble for delayed replies, no Select, Read or Kill. The
; RN16 is a 16-bit LFSR step mixed with NOW, not a true random source.
;
; Memory (data words at BASE, thread 3's quarter top): +0 the prefix word
; of an RN16 reply, +1 RN16, +2 0x8000 (its dummy bit), +3 the prefix word of
; an EPC reply, +4 PC, +5.. EPC, then PacketCRC and 0x8000; +16 TICK_INT of
; the reply, +17 TICK_FRAC, +18 ONES (a half-bit's toggle pattern), +19 the
; Query's first 8 bits (1000 DR M TRext), +20 T1 lead, +21 state (0
; arbitrate, 1 reply), +22 TRcal in clocks, +23 bits of the EPC reply,
; +24 THR, +25 VIDX (the preamble's special bits, at "send" below).
;
; Registers, receiving: r0 the bits, r1 the last rise, r2 the interval, r3
; RTcal, r4 the timeout (1.5 or 3 RTcal), r5 bits so far, r6 the
; command's length, r7 scratch.
; Sending: r0 the word, r1 half-bits left, r2 the next word, r3 the line,
; r4 the last bit, r5 bits left in r0, r6 BASE, r7 the pattern.
;
; Size: 355 words, 0x000-0x162: it spills over thread 1 and 2's quarters
; (the listing says so); the tag runs alone, on thread 0. Data at 0x1E0-0x1F9.
; Timing: the half-cycle loop's longest stretch is 29 slots (116 clocks) and
; the first, from the new grid, 30 (120): --strict proves both at a 128-clock
; half (worst slack 9 clocks), so every staged edge lands on its tick.

        .imem   512                     ; the macro build: quarters of 128 words
        .thread 0
        .pins   ENV = IN0, BS = OUT0

        .equ    HMIN = 128              ; clocks: shorter half cycles are refused
        .tick   HMIN                    ; the shortest half cycle sent (header)
        .equ    BASE = 0x1E0
        .equ    LAG = 12                ; clocks from the T1 wait to the new grid
        .equ    PATF = 0xBB20           ; FM0 preamble: toggle (1) or hold, a half

        SETP    BS, 0                   ; no backscatter
        .csr    BE_PINS, 15             ; SHO drives no pin (6.3)
        .csr    BE_CFG, 0x202           ; CRC_EN, MSB first
        .csr    CRC_POLY, 0x1021        ; x^16 + x^12 + x^5 + 1 (Table 6-11)
        .csr    CRC_INIT, 0xFFFF
        MOV16   r6, BASE
        POP     r0                      ; 1. the RN16 seed
        ST      r0, r6, 1
        MOV16   r0, 0x8000
        ST      r0, r6, 2
        POP     r1                      ; 2. N
        MOV     r2, r1
        SHLI    r2, 11                  ; PC: L = N
        ST      r2, r6, 4
        CRCI
        LDSR    r2
        CALL    sh16
        MOV     r3, r6
        ADDI    r3, 5
        MOV     r4, r1
cfg:    POP     r0                      ; 3. the EPC words
        ST      r0, r3, 0
        LDSR    r0
        CALL    sh16
        ADDI    r3, 1
        DJNZ    r4, cfg
        STCRC   r0
        NOT     r0, r0                  ; ones-complement (6.3.1.5)
        ST      r0, r3, 0
        MOV16   r0, 0x8000
        ST      r0, r3, 1
        ADDI    r1, 2
        SHLI    r1, 4
        ADDI    r1, 1                   ; PC, EPC, CRC and the dummy bit
        ST      r1, r6, 23
        LDI     r0, 0
        ST      r0, r6, 21              ; arbitrate
        ST      r0, r6, 22              ; no TRcal yet: a reply is refused
        .csr    BE_CFG, 0x200           ; CRC_EN, LSB first: SHO takes SR[0]
        .csr    CRC_POLY, 0x4800        ; x^5 + x^3 + 1, left-aligned (Table 6-12)
        .csr    CRC_INIT, 0x4800        ; preset 01001

; ---------------------------------------------------------------- receive
idle:   WAITP   ENV, 1                  ; CW
        WAITP   ENV, 0                  ; the delimiter
        WAITP   ENV, 1
        CSRR    r1, NOW
        CALL    edge                    ; data-0
        CALL    edge                    ; RTcal
        MOV     r3, r2
        ADD     r4, r2, r2
        ADD     r4, r4, r2              ; TRcal is up to 3 RTcal (eq. 2)
        CALL    edget
        BT      idle
        LDI     r0, 0
        LDI     r5, 0
        CRCI
        MOV     r4, r3
        SHRI    r4, 1
        ADD     r4, r4, r3              ; 1.5 RTcal: the end of a frame
        CMP     r2, r3
        BNC     bit                     ; shorter than RTcal: frame-sync, a bit
        MOV16   r6, BASE
        ST      r2, r6, 22              ; TRcal: a preamble
        CALL    edget
        BT      idle
bit:    SHLI    r0, 1
        SHLI    r2, 1
        CMP     r2, r3                  ; C = (interval >= pivot): data-1
        BNC     b0
        ORI     r0, 1
b0:     LDSR    r0
        SHO                             ; the bit through the CRC-5
        ADDI    r5, 1
        CMPI    r5, 2
        BNZ     b4
        CMPI    r0, 1
        BZ      isack
        CMPI    r0, 2
        BNZ     skip                    ; 00, 11: not ours
        LDI     r6, 4
        JMP     nb
isack:  LDI     r6, 18
        JMP     nb
b4:     CMP     r5, r6
        BZ      fin
        CMPI    r5, 8
        BNZ     nb
        CMPI    r6, 22                  ; a Query (not an ACK's 8th bit)
        BNZ     nb
        MOV16   r7, BASE
        ST      r0, r7, 19              ; 1000 DR M TRext
nb:     CALL    edget
        BT      idle                    ; the frame ended early
        JMP     bit
fin:    CMPI    r5, 4
        BNZ     fin2
        CMPI    r0, 8
        BNZ     skip                    ; 10xx but not Query
        LDI     r6, 22
        JMP     nb
fin2:   CMPI    r5, 18
        BZ      ack
        JMP     query
skip:   CALL    edget                   ; to the end of the frame
        BT      idle
        JMP     skip

; edget: the next rising edge, or T after 1.5 RTcal with no falling edge;
; edge: the same without a timeout. r2 = the interval, r1 = the new rise.
edget:  MOV     r7, r4
        ADD     r7, r7, r1
        CSRW    TD, r7
        WAITP   ENV, 0, T
        BT      eret
e1:     WAITP   ENV, 1
        CSRR    r7, NOW
        SUB     r2, r7, r1
        MOV     r1, r7
eret:   RET
edge:   WAITP   ENV, 0
        JMP     e1
sh16:   LDI     r7, 16                  ; 16 bits of SR through the CRC
sh:     SHO
        DJNZ    r7, sh
        RET


; ------------------------------------------------------------------ Query
query:  STCRC   r7
        CMPI    r7, 0                   ; residue 00000 (Annex F.1)
        BNZ     arb                     ; a CRC-5 error: invalid, ignored
        MOV16   r6, BASE
        LD      r2, r6, 1               ; RN16: an LFSR step mixed with NOW
        CSRR    r7, NOW
        XOR     r2, r2, r7
        SHRI    r2, 1
        BNC     q1
        MOV16   r7, 0xB400
        XOR     r2, r2, r7
q1:     ST      r2, r6, 1
        MOV     r7, r0
        SHRI    r7, 5
        ANDI    r7, 15                  ; Q
        LDI     r5, 1
        SHL     r5, r5, r7
        SUBI    r5, 1
        AND     r5, r5, r2              ; the slot, 0 .. 2^Q - 1, from the RN16
        BNZ     arb                     ; not slot 0: silent for the round
        LD      r2, r6, 22              ; TRcal, clocks
        LD      r4, r6, 19              ; 1000 DR M TRext
        MOV     r7, r4
        ANDI    r7, 8
        BNZ     dr64
        MOV     r5, r2                  ; DR = 8: half = TRcal / 16
        SHRI    r5, 4
        MOV     r7, r2
        ANDI    r7, 15
        SHLI    r7, 4
        ST      r7, r6, 17
        MOV     r7, r2
        SHRI    r7, 2
        ADD     r2, r2, r7              ; 10 Tpri = 20 halves = 5 TRcal / 4
        JMP     q2
dr64:   MOV     r7, r2                  ; DR = 64/3: half = 3 TRcal / 128
        ADD     r2, r2, r7
        ADD     r2, r2, r7
        MOV     r5, r2
        SHRI    r5, 7
        MOV     r7, r2
        SHLI    r7, 9
        SHRI    r7, 8
        ST      r7, r6, 17
        MOV     r7, r2
        SHRI    r7, 3
        SHRI    r2, 5
        ADD     r2, r2, r7              ; 20 halves = 5 (3 TRcal) / 32
q2:     LDI     r7, HMIN
        CMP     r5, r7
        BNC     arb                     ; BLF too high: refused, silent
        ST      r5, r6, 16
        CMP     r2, r3
        BC      q3
        MOV     r2, r3                  ; T1 = MAX(RTcal, 10 Tpri)
q3:     SUB     r2, r2, r5              ; the first edge is a half after the grid
        SUBI    r2, LAG
        ST      r2, r6, 20
        MOV     r7, r4
        SHRI    r7, 1
        ANDI    r7, 3                   ; M: 0 FM0, 1..3 Miller 2, 4, 8
        LDI     r5, 1
        SHL     r5, r5, r7              ; K halves a half-bit
        ADDI    r5, 1
        MOV16   r7, 0xFFFF
        SHR     r7, r7, r5
        NOT     r7, r7                  ; ONES: K toggles and the end mark
        ST      r7, r6, 18
        LDI     r7, 1
        ST      r7, r6, 21              ; reply
        ADD     r2, r2, r1
        CSRW    TD, r2                  ; T1 after the last rise
        MOV     r2, r6
        ADDI    r2, 1                   ; RN16 and its dummy bit
        LDI     r1, 17
        JMP     tx

; -------------------------------------------------------------------- ACK
ack:    MOV16   r6, BASE
        LD      r7, r6, 21
        CMPI    r7, 0
        BZ      arb                     ; no RN16 out: ignored
        LD      r7, r6, 1
        CMP     r7, r0                  ; the echoed RN16
        BNZ     arb
        LD      r2, r6, 20
        ADD     r2, r2, r1
        CSRW    TD, r2
        LD      r1, r6, 23
        MOV     r2, r6
        ADDI    r2, 4                   ; PC, EPC, PacketCRC, dummy
        JMP     tx
arb:    MOV16   r6, BASE
        LDI     r7, 0
        ST      r7, r6, 21
        JMP     idle

; --------------------------------------------------------------------- send
; In: r2 = the first data word, r1 = data bits (with the dummy), TD = the
; T1 target in clocks. The preamble is sent as bits ahead of the data: its
; first bits preloaded in r0, the rest (TRext) in the prefix word before the
; data. Two bits are special: FM0's v (a 1 without its boundary toggle,
; VIDX) and Miller's pilot (zeros that keep their boundary toggles, THR).
; Every half-bit plays ONES (K toggles then an end mark), its first toggle
; cleared by the rules: FM0 boundary never (but v), middle of a 1; Miller
; boundary between two 0s, middle of a 1. r1 counts half-bits: odd after
; the decrement is a boundary, even a middle.
tx:     LD      r7, r6, 19              ; 1000 DR M TRext
        MOV     r3, r7
        ANDI    r3, 6
        BNZ     smil
        ANDI    r7, 1                   ; FM0
        BZ      sf0
        LDI     r0, 0x2B                ; 12 zeros, 1 0 1 0 v 1: 18 bits
        SUBI    r2, 1
        ST      r0, r2, 0
        LDI     r0, 0
        LDI     r5, 2
        ADDI    r1, 18
        LDI     r3, 16                  ; v is bit 16
        JMP     sfc
sf0:    MOV16   r0, 0xAC00              ; 1 0 1 0 v 1
        LDI     r5, 6
        ADDI    r1, 6
        LDI     r3, 4
sfc:    SHLI    r1, 1
        SHLI    r3, 1
        ADDI    r3, 1
        SUB     r7, r1, r3
        ST      r7, r6, 25              ; VIDX = 2N - 1 - 2i
        LDI     r7, 0
        ST      r7, r6, 24              ; THR 0: FM0 never clears a boundary
        JMP     sgo
smil:   ANDI    r7, 1                   ; Miller
        BZ      sm0
        LDI     r0, 0x17                ; 16 zeros of pilot, 010111: 22 bits
        SUBI    r2, 1
        ST      r0, r2, 0
        LDI     r0, 0
        LDI     r5, 6
        ADDI    r1, 22
        LDI     r3, 16
        JMP     smc
sm0:    MOV16   r0, 0x05C0              ; 4 zeros of pilot, 010111
        LDI     r5, 10
        ADDI    r1, 10
        LDI     r3, 4
smc:    SHLI    r1, 1
        SHLI    r3, 1
        ADDI    r3, 1
        SUB     r7, r1, r3
        ST      r7, r6, 24              ; THR = 2N - 2 pilot - 1: through 010's 0
        MOV16   r7, 0xFFFF
        ST      r7, r6, 25              ; no v
sgo:    LD      r4, r6, 17
        LD      r3, r6, 16
        WAITD   0                       ; T1 less a half cycle
        CSRW    TICK_FRAC, r4
        CSRW    TICK_INT, r3            ; the grid restarts here (SEMANTICS 4)
        SETD    0
        LDI     r3, 0                   ; the line is 0
        LDI     r4, 1
        JMP     refill                  ; the first bit

hw:     WAITD   1                       ; one half cycle
hl:     SHLI    r7, 1                   ; C = toggle; Z = the end mark went
        BZ      refill
        BNC     hw
tg:     XORI    r3, 1
        BZ      hz
        SETP    BS, 1, D
        JMP     hw
hz:     SETP    BS, 0, D
        JMP     hw
hf:     SHLI    r7, 1                   ; a half-bit's first half: never the mark
        BNC     hw
        JMP     tg

refill: SUBI    r1, 1
        BNC     tend                    ; no half-bits left
        MOV     r7, r1
        ANDI    r7, 1
        BZ      mid
        SHLI    r0, 1                   ; a boundary: C = the next bit
        BC      rone
        CMPI    r4, 0
        BNZ     rz1                     ; 0 after 1: toggle
        LD      r7, r6, 24
        CMP     r1, r7
        BC      rz1                     ; FM0, or the pilot: toggle
        LD      r7, r6, 18
        SHLI    r7, 1                   ; 0 after 0 (Miller): no toggle
        SHRI    r7, 1
        LDI     r4, 0
        JMP     hf
rz1:    LD      r7, r6, 18
        LDI     r4, 0
        JMP     hf
rone:   LD      r7, r6, 25
        CMP     r1, r7
        LD      r7, r6, 18
        LDI     r4, 1
        BNZ     hf
        SHLI    r7, 1                   ; FM0's v: no boundary toggle
        SHRI    r7, 1
        JMP     hf
mid:    DJNZ    r5, m1                  ; r0 empty after this bit: the next word
        LD      r0, r2, 0
        ADDI    r2, 1
        LDI     r5, 16
m1:     LD      r7, r6, 18
        CMPI    r4, 0
        BZ      hf                      ; the middle of a 0: toggle
        SHLI    r7, 1                   ; the middle of a 1: none
        SHRI    r7, 1
        JMP     hf

tend:   SETP    BS, 0, D                ; after the dummy bit: back to 0
        WAITD   1
        LDI     r7, 0
        CSRW    TICK_FRAC, r7
        LDI     r7, 1
        CSRW    TICK_INT, r7            ; tick = 1 clock again
        JMP     idle
